        "original_id": "62878273-6da3-5dee-bb0b-0dbfee71140d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee, North Carolina; Cherokee County, North Carolina; Swain County, North Carolina; Graham County, North Carolina; North Carolina, United States\n- Dams: Hiwassee Dam; Fontana Dam; Watauga Dam\n- Water Systems: Tennessee Valley Authority system; Little Tennessee River; Hiwassee River; Hiwassee Reservoir\n\nFacts:\n- Fontana Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States.\n- Hiwassee Dam is 307 feet tall and is the third highest dam in the Tennessee Valley Authority system, behind only Fontana Dam and Watauga Dam.\n- Hiwassee is a small village in Cherokee County, North Carolina, located next to Hiwassee Dam and the artificial Hiwassee Reservoir on the Hiwassee River.",
